    <bpmn:process id="W_W3874" name="W3874. Fraud Recovery, Restitution &amp; Asset Recovery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Confirmed loss case (links to W3873)
Frequency: Continuous
Volume: Recovery target ~20–50% of confirmed fraud loss
Owner: Fraud Management / Finance / Legal
Participants: Fraud Management, Finance/AR (links to VS-16/VS-17), Legal (links to VS-100), Collections (links to VS-16), LP (links to VS-23), Treasury (links to VS-18), Insurance (links to VS-26)
Source: workflow W3874 — Fraud Recovery, Restitution &amp; Asset Recovery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3874_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3874_Lane1" name="Fraud Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3874_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3874_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3874_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3874_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3874_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3874_Start3" name="Confirmed loss case (links to W3873)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3874_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3874_Task4" name="Fraud Management/Finance quantify recoverable loss (principal + cost), identify…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fraud Management/Finance quantify recoverable loss (principal + cost), identify recovery sources (customer account balance/points/gift balance offset links to VS-13/VS-54, restitution agreement, civil/criminal recovery links to VS-100, insurance claim links to VS-26, vendor/3P recovery), and prioritize by quantum
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Finance / Legal
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3874_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3874_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3874_Task5" name="Fraud Management/Legal/Collections pursue recovery: demand letters, restitution…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fraud Management/Legal/Collections pursue recovery: demand letters, restitution agreements, account-offset, small-claims/civil action where material, and coordinate with law-enforcement asset recovery (links to W3877)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Legal / Collections
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3874_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3874_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3874_Task6" name="Fraud Management/Finance/Treasury record recoveries against the original loss…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Fraud Management/Finance/Treasury record recoveries against the original loss (links to VS-17 GL), report net loss-rate (links to W3880), and recover via insurance where applicable (links to VS-26/W26.3)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Finance / Treasury
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3874_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3874_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3874_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3874_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3874_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-606 (ensure controlled execution — Investigation, Recovery, Compliance &amp; Analytics (PA-125.3).) | - operational: account-offset and prioritized civil action; operational: subrogation coordination (links to VS-26)
Owner: Fraud Management / Finance / Legal</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3874_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3874_Annotation8" targetRef="W3874_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
