    <bpmn:process id="W_W3876" name="W3876. Internal / Employee Fraud &amp; Collusion Investigation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Employee-fraud alert (links to W3865/W3860); tip-off (links to VS-119)
Frequency: Continuous (~6,911 employees + ~10–20% contingent)
Volume: ~50–200 employee-fraud cases/yr
Owner: Fraud Management / LP / HR / Internal Audit
Participants: Fraud Management, LP (links to VS-23), Internal Audit (links to VS-21), HR (links to VS-19/VS-103), Legal (links to VS-100), IT Security (links to VS-27.3), Store Ops (links to VS-07), Speak-Up (links to VS-119)
Source: workflow W3876 — Internal / Employee Fraud &amp; Collusion Investigation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3876_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3876_Lane1" name="Fraud Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3876_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3876_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3876_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3876_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3876_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3876_Start3" name="Employee-fraud alert (links to W3865/W3860); tip-off (links to VS-119)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3876_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3876_Task4" name="Fraud Management/LP/Internal-Audit investigate employee fraud: cashier…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fraud Management/LP/Internal-Audit investigate employee fraud: cashier theft/sweethearting (links to W3865), refund/void manipulation, expense/P-card fraud (links to VS-34.3), procurement kickback/vendor collusion (links to VS-15/VS-86.3), data/credential misuse (links to VS-27.3), and vendor-side collusion with buyers
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / LP / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3876_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3876_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3876_Task5" name="Fraud Management/HR/Legal handle employment-aspect: due-process (NLRC/DOLE —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fraud Management/HR/Legal handle employment-aspect: due-process (NLRC/DOLE — links to VS-84), administrative investigation, evidence preservation, suspension/termination decision, and restitution/recovery (links to W3874); coordinate with speak-up confidentiality (links to VS-119) and retaliation protection
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / HR / Legal
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead / CHRO
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3876_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3876_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3876_Task6" name="Fraud Management/Internal-Audit report material employee fraud to the Audit…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Fraud Management/Internal-Audit report material employee fraud to the Audit Committee (links to VS-21/VS-36), refer for prosecution where material (links to W3877), and close control gaps (segregation of duties links to W1408, access reviews links to VS-27)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3876_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3876_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
