    <bpmn:process id="W_W3880" name="W3880. Fraud Analytics, Loss Rates &amp; Program KPI Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly/quarterly close; strategy review
Frequency: Monthly + quarterly
Volume: Enterprise fraud scorecard (~10–15 KPIs by channel)
Owner: Fraud Management / Insights
Participants: Fraud Management, Insights (links to VS-28.1), Finance (links to VS-17.4), Risk/Internal Audit (links to VS-21), Channels (links to VS-07/VS-10/VS-80/VS-13), Strategy (links to VS-33), Data Science (links to VS-30.2)
Source: workflow W3880 — Fraud Analytics, Loss Rates &amp; Program KPI Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3880_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3880_Lane1" name="Fraud Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3880_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3880_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3880_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3880_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3880_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3880_Start3" name="Monthly/quarterly close; strategy review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3880_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3880_Task4" name="Fraud Management/Insights produce the monthly fraud scorecard: gross/net loss…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fraud Management/Insights produce the monthly fraud scorecard: gross/net loss by channel and typology, loss-rate (% of revenue/transactions), chargeback rate, recovery rate, false-positive rate, case SLA, model performance — reconciled to shrink (links to VS-23) and revenue assurance (links to VS-118) to avoid double-count
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Insights
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3880_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3880_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3880_Task5" name="Fraud Management/Finance/Risk roll up to the enterprise fraud-loss rate vs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fraud Management/Finance/Risk roll up to the enterprise fraud-loss rate vs appetite (links to W3857), quantify financial impact on EBITDA (links to VS-17.4), and brief the Audit &amp; Risk Committee (links to VS-21/VS-36)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Finance / Risk
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3880_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3880_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3880_Task6" name="Fraud Management/Strategy use analytics to reallocate controls/spend to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Fraud Management/Strategy use analytics to reallocate controls/spend to highest-loss channels, prioritize detection backlog (links to W3859), and drive continuous improvement of the program
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Strategy / Data Science
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3880_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3880_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3880_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3880_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3880_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-606 (ensure controlled execution — Investigation, Recovery, Compliance &amp; Analytics (PA-125.3).) | - operational: reconciled taxonomy; operational: near-real-time loss dashboards
Owner: Fraud Management / Insights</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
